35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The roads were closed eleven days, but the community halls kept their evening timetables. They are resilient.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The outer wards lost their bus link. Residents face an hour's round trip to any staffed counter.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The digitisation project failed, but the partner-run evening groups still meet unaided. People want connection.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant only pays for twelve months. After that, the flat budget carries the cost. That is a trap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"We have retired tradespeople, but no one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, that is a serious barrier. If they cannot get here, we are not serving them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, exactly. The geography is fixed. We must go to them or find a way that doesn't rely on buses.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, that is a gap. But the associations are already running their own sessions. They have the skills.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the partner groups are a good sign. But if the grant ends, who pays for the facilitators?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the associations staff their own sessions. They are self-sufficient. We just need to support them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Rin, the attendance sheets show forty visitors a session in the outer wards. That is high demand.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, high demand, but no access. A mobile service could bridge that gap without relying on buses.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, a mobile service? That sounds like the outreach stops. But the equipment lines overran by a third.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the vehicle costs are a risk. But the grant covers the first year. We just need to plan for year two.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the mobile service needs drivers and staff. Do we have the skills? The register is thin.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I am leaning towards a service that reaches the outer wards. The community halls are a good model.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. A mobile branch could visit the outer wards on a fixed schedule. It solves the access problem.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I like the idea of going to them. But we must be careful with the costs. The equipment overran last year.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I will weigh the grant terms against the mobile service costs. It is a tight fit, but possible.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,I will check if the volunteer register can cover the mobile service. We need reliable people.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
