60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,The candidates are here. A is a mobile branch. B is a maker workshop. C is language circles. D is a digital archive.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, A directly addresses the access issue I found. The outer wards need a service that comes to them.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, A is like the outreach stops. But the equipment costs were high. Is it worth the risk?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the grant covers the first year. The risk is in year two. But the demand is real.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the mobile service needs staff. The volunteer register has retired tradespeople, but not drivers.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, the community halls have staff. We could partner with them. They are already running evening sessions.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that is a good idea. The halls are resilient. They can host the mobile branch.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, the partner-run groups are a good model. But the digitisation project failed. We must be careful.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the digitisation project was a one-off. The mobile service is ongoing. The grant supports it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the ongoing cost is the problem. But the associations are self-sufficient. We can learn from them.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I think A is the best choice. It reaches the people who need us most. The community halls are ready.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. A solves the access problem. The outer wards are cut off. We must go to them.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I am still worried about the costs. But the demand is high. Let’s try A.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I will vote for A. The grant covers the first year. We can plan for year two.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I will vote for A. The associations can help. We have the community support.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am happy we are all leaning towards A. It is the right choice for our community.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. A is the logical solution to the access problem. I vote for A.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I vote for A. Let’s hope the costs stay under control.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for A. The data supports it. The demand is real.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for A. The community is ready. We have the support.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
